  "id": "COMPOUND:16986 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions involving the compound (10S,11R,12R,15S)-3,4,5,11,12,13,21,22,23,26,27,38,39-tridecahydroxy-9,14,17,29,36-pentaoxaoctacyclo[29.8.0.02,7.010,15.019,24.025,34.028,33.032,37]nonatriaconta-1(39),2,4,6,19,21,23,25,27,31,33,37-dodecaene-8,18,30,35-tetrone and the proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src. The compound is linked to multiple targets, including Myosin light chain kinase 3, Phosphorylase b kinase gamma catalytic chain, and Non-receptor tyrosine-protein kinase TNK1, all of which are known to interact with Src. These interactions are supported by evidence from different pathways, indicating that the compound may act as a modulator of Src activity through various mechanisms. The evidence suggests that the compound may influence Src through either direct binding or through downstream signaling pathways, but the exact mechanism remains unclear. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with varying scores across the paths, and further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the direct relationship between the compound and Src.",
